course: dictionary
lesson: 4502
title: Working out a word from its parts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hawksbill is a kind of sea turtle, and its name gives you clues. The word hawk is hiding in it, and the dictionary says its beak is narrow and curved like a hawk's. So the name tells you what the beak looks like.
explain: «Hawksbill turtles eat sponges that many other animals cannot eat.» The words hawksbill turtles tell you this is a kind of turtle. The rest of the sentence tells you what it does: it eats sponges. You can work out a lot from one sentence.
explain: Check your guess by putting it back into the sentence. A sea turtle with a hooked beak fits, so your meaning makes sense. If it does not fit, look for more clues or use a dictionary.
fact: A hawksbill is a sea turtle with a narrow beak curved like a hawk's.
fact: Hawksbills live on coral reefs in warm seas.
fact: A hawksbill is critically endangered, which means it is at very high risk of dying out.
fact: «Hawksbill turtles eat sponges that many other animals cannot eat, and this helps corals have more space to grow.»
exercise: What is a hawksbill? | A fish that lives in rivers | A kind of coral that grows in warm seas | A bird that catches fish with its beak | *A sea turtle with a narrow, curved beak
exercise: «Hawksbill turtles eat sponges that many other animals cannot eat.» What do hawksbills eat? | *Sponges | Shells | Bread crumbs | Grass
exercise: The word hawk is part of hawksbill. What does it tell you about the hawksbill's beak? | *It is curved like a hawk's | It is soft and round | It is bright red | It is very long and straight
test: «Hawksbills live on coral reefs in warm seas.» Where do hawksbills live? | In deserts | *On coral reefs in warm seas | In cold rivers | On mountains
test: The hawksbill is critically endangered. What does endangered mean? | Living only in the dark | Able to fly | *At risk of dying out | Very common
exam: What does the word hawksbill mean? | A hawk that lives in the sea | A fish with sharp teeth | A coral reef in warm seas | *A sea turtle with a narrow beak curved like a hawk's
